    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0075" n="65" xml:id="pg65"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/3–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-06T15:00:00+07:00">March 2, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 2—1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>346. The bipartisan character of the American delegation to the forthcoming San
                    Francisco Conference has aroused considerable interest in Chinese official and
                    unofficial circles here with the result that it is now reported without
                    confirmation that consideration is being [given] the possible taking of a
                    semblance of similar action by the Chinese Government. It is generally accepted
                    that the Chinese delegation will be headed by T. V. Soong and will include
                    Wellington Koo<anchor n="95" xml:id="d33-f1"/> and Victor Hoo.<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d33-f2"/> It is rumored that Hu Shih<anchor n="97" xml:id="d33-f3"/>
                    may also be named as a gesture toward the liberals and that with a view to
                    finding favor with a large section of the American press as well as to
                    offsetting Communist demands for representation, two PPC members may be chosen
                    including Lin Tsu-han,<anchor n="98" xml:id="d33-f4"/> the Communists’ usual
                    representative in Chungking.</p>
                <p>Among other reports arising from questions having relation to the San Francisco
                    Conference is one that Sun Fo may go to Russia on special mission rather than T.
                    V. Soong. Another is that the Generalissimo has asked the President to meet him
                    before the Conference at some place in Australia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d33-f1" n="95" xml:id="d33-f1-content">
